  [1mThe design[0m

  Plain HTML + a few lines of vanilla JS in [38;5;153mindex.html[39m (no build step, matching what's there):

  - A [38;5;153m<label>[39m wrapping [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m plus the item text, inside [38;5;153m<main>[39m.
  - A [38;5;153mchange[39m listener toggles a [38;5;153mdone[39m class on the label; a small [38;5;153m<style>[39m block gives [38;5;153m.done[39m a line-through and muted
    color.
  - State lives only in the DOM — no storage, no framework, no dependencies.
  - Testing: none added — there's no test setup in the repo. Verification is opening the page and clicking.

  The one fork that changes the output: what the checkbox is attached to. The page has no task items yet, so I need to
  know whether to invent some.
